        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T18:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason I named this function sk_doubles_nearly_equal_ulps instead of a more generic sk_doubles_nearly_equal is that it is *not* a more generic function.\n\nAs per https://randomascii.wordpress.com/2012/02/25/comparing-floating-point-numbers-2012-edition/\n\"If you are comparing two arbitrary numbers that could be zero or non-zero then you need the kitchen sink. Good luck\"\n\nWe certainly could have that generic sk_doubles_nearly_equal, but that requires a bit more careful thought.",
      "parentUuid": "d7513d9d_6c7ec337",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 42,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "f5355a0a2d41376399c58a08f2879c02d7eac04a",
